title: CPS Reformation
subtitle: The Communist Party of Sordland is becoming the People's Party of Sordland.
view-if: year = 1951 and month = 2 and cps_party_leader = "Lackber" and pro_republic >= 70
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: cps_name = "PPS"; ddp_dstp_seen = 1; new_middle_kpd += 3; old_middle_kpd += 1; worker_kpd += 5
tags: event

= CPS Reformation

Leaders of the Communist Party, seeing the party's vote share not increasing, have decided that now is the time to reform the party further. The party leader, Erwin Lackber, has engineered a new big tent leftist party, though the communists still remain. Now, the party will be called the People's Party of Sordland, or PPS.

This has led to outcry from the left wing of the party, malyenvists who would rather not work with Left Democrats. However this massively increases the appeal of the party to more moderate leftists and the workers who would usually vote for us. [? if ideology = "socdem": Erwin has also expressed interest in forming a Popular Front.?]

- @advantage: We must increase our appeal to the workers.
- @nothing: This is none of our concern.

@advantage
choose-if: resources >= 2
subtitle: -2 resources 
on-arrival: worker_spd += 2*(1-dissent); resources -= 2

By losing the votes of the workers we risk losing seats in the next election. Resources will have to be spent however.


@nothing

The PPS's internal affairs are none of our concern.
